{
  "name": "Uptime check to Telegram alert",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "sticky-overview",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -340,
        120
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 460,
        "height": 760,
        "content": "### Who's it for\nAnyone self-hosting a service who wants to know the moment it goes down - without paying for uptime monitoring.\n\n### How it works\nEvery 5 minutes a Schedule Trigger runs. The Config node holds the URL, service name and Telegram chat id. An HTTP Request checks the endpoint with a 10-second timeout and neverError enabled, so a timeout becomes data instead of a crashed run. An IF node tests whether the status code is greater than 399; if it is, a Telegram node sends a Markdown alert with the service name, status code, URL and timestamp. When the check passes, a NoOp node ends the run silently - no success spam.\n\n### How to set up\n1. Import the workflow.\n2. Open the Config node and set url, serviceName and chatId. Alternatively point them at the HTTP_URL, SERVICE_NAME and TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID environment variables so no value is stored in the workflow itself.\n3. Create a Telegram credential with your bot token from BotFather and select it on the Alert Telegram node.\n4. Activate the workflow.\n\n### Requirements\nn8n (self-hosted or cloud - built and tested on 2.35.x) and a Telegram bot token.\n\n### How to customize\nChange the interval on the Schedule Trigger, add more items to Config to monitor several services, or replace the Telegram node with Slack, Discord or email."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "sticky-step1",
      "name": "Step 1 - Every 5 minutes",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        180,
        60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 260,
        "height": 180,
        "content": "Runs the check on a fixed interval."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "sticky-step2",
      "name": "Step 2 - Set what to watch",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        420,
        60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 280,
        "height": 180,
        "content": "Set the URL, service name and Telegram chat id here."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "sticky-step3",
      "name": "Step 3 - Check and branch",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        640,
        60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 300,
        "height": 180,
        "content": "HTTP check, then an IF that fires only on a bad status."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "sticky-step4",
      "name": "Step 4 - Alert",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1080,
        60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 300,
        "height": 180,
        "content": "Telegram message on failure; silent NoOp on success."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "schedule-1",
      "name": "Every 5 Minutes",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "position": [
        220,
        300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "minutes",
              "minutesInterval": 5
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "config-1",
      "name": "Config",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "notes": "Edit these three values (or point them at env: HTTP_URL, SERVICE_NAME, TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID).",
      "position": [
        440,
        300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "cfg-url",
              "name": "url",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "https://example.com/health"
            },
            {
              "id": "cfg-name",
              "name": "serviceName",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "My Service"
            },
            {
              "id": "cfg-chat",
              "name": "chatId",
              "type": "string",
              "value": ""
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 3.4
    },
    {
      "id": "http-1",
      "name": "Check Endpoint",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput",
      "position": [
        660,
        300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "url": "={{ $json.url }}",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 10000,
          "response": {
            "response": {
              "neverError": true,
              "fullResponse": true
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 4.2
    },
    {
      "id": "if-1",
      "name": "Is Down?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "position": [
        880,
        300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "version": 2,
            "leftValue": "",
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "typeValidation": "loose"
          },
          "combinator": "or",
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "cond-status",
              "operator": {
                "type": "number",
                "operation": "gt"
              },
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.statusCode }}",
              "rightValue": 399
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 2.2
    },
    {
      "id": "tg-1",
      "name": "Alert Telegram",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.telegram",
      "notes": "Create a Telegram credential (bot token) and set it on this node.",
      "position": [
        1120,
        200
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "text": "=\ud83d\udd34 *{{ $('Config').item.json.serviceName }}* is DOWN\nHTTP: {{ $json.statusCode }}\nURL: {{ $('Config').item.json.url }}\nChecked: {{ $now.toISO() }}",
        "chatId": "={{ $('Config').item.json.chatId }}",
        "additionalFields": {
          "parse_mode": "Markdown"
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "noop-1",
      "name": "OK - No Action",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.noOp",
      "position": [
        1120,
        420
      ],
      "parameters": {},
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
  ],
  "pinData": {},
  "settings": {
    "executionOrder": "v1"
  },
  "connections": {
    "Config": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Check Endpoint",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Is Down?": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Alert Telegram",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "node": "OK - No Action",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Check Endpoint": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Is Down?",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Every 5 Minutes": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Config",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    }
  }
}